{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5631: implement `cmd/chronic/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. This is a stitch task in generation run 44. The specific requirements are to implement srd112-chronic R1.1, R1.2, and R1.3:\n   - R1.1: Execute a COMMAND with arguments, capturing stdout and stderr. If COMMAND exits 0, suppress all output. If non-zero exit, write captured stdout to stdout and captured stderr to stderr.\n   - R1.2: `-e` or `--stderr` flag triggers output display when the command writes to stderr, even if it exits 0.\n   - R1.3: `-v` or `--verbose` prints the command being run to stderr before execution.\n   \n   Additional SRD requirements (R2.1-R2.3) govern exit codes and SIGPIPE handling which are needed for correct behavior even though the task title only mentions R1.1-R1.3.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `chronic` is a moreutils utility that runs commands silently unless they fail\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew reference binary (`chronic` from moreutils)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `os/exec` for running child commands and capturing stdout/stderr\n   - Exit code 100 when COMMAND cannot be found/executed (R2.2)\n   - Exit with COMMAND's exit status (R2.1)\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - Must write all files before running build/test\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd112-chronic.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining chronic's behavior. Key requirements:\n     - R1.1: Capture stdout/stderr; suppress on exit 0, display on non-zero exit\n     - R1.2: `-e`/`--stderr` triggers output if stderr is non-empty even on exit 0\n     - R1.3: `-v`/`--verbose` prints command to stderr before execution\n     - R2.1: Exit with COMMAND's exit status\n     - R2.2: Exit 100 when COMMAND not found\n     - R2.3: SIGPIPE via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n     - Non-goals: no timeout or resource limits\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   \n   - `cmd/chronic/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The main implementation file for the chronic utility\n     - Must be created from scratch\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` which must be called at start of main\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements for R1.1, R1.2, R1.3\n   - Was about to plan the implementation approach and write the code\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with full project context, SRDs, source code, architecture, execution constitution, go style constitution, and the specific task to implement cmd/chronic with requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 from srd112-chronic.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/chronic/main.go` implementing R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 (and R2.1-R2.3 for correct behavior)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/chronic ./cmd/chronic/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/chronic/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC5 are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd112-chronic.yaml` and was about to plan and implement `cmd/chronic/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The SRD reading revealed the full requirements:\n   - R1.1: Execute command, capture stdout/stderr, suppress on success, display on failure\n   - R1.2: `-e`/`--stderr` flag triggers output when stderr is non-empty even on exit 0\n   - R1.3: `-v`/`--verbose` prints command to stderr before execution\n   - R2.1: Exit with command's exit status\n   - R2.2: Exit 100 when command not found\n   - R2.3: SIGPIPE handling via InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/chronic/main.go` implementing the chronic utility. The implementation should:\n   - Start with copyright header and package main\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Parse `-e`/`--stderr` and `-v`/`--verbose` flags manually (no cobra needed for this simple utility)\n   - Execute the command using `os/exec`, capturing stdout and stderr to buffers\n   - On exit 0: suppress output (unless `-e` and stderr is non-empty)\n   - On non-zero exit: write captured stdout to os.Stdout, captured stderr to os.Stderr\n   - Exit with command's exit status, or 100 if command not found\n   - Then run `go build -o bin/chronic ./cmd/chronic/` and `go vet ./cmd/chronic/...`\n   \n   The task description states: \"Implement srd112-chronic R1.1 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd112-chronic R1.2 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd112-chronic R1.3 as specified in the SRD\" with acceptance criteria requiring build success, vet clean, and each requirement implemented.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5631/68705226-65db-4758-9